The direct sum and telescoped harmonic expression are two views of one quantity. {{demo:0}}

<details><summary>Reveal the finite theorem and proof</summary>For every $n\ge0$, summing $1/(k+1)-\log((k+2)/(k+1))$ from $k=0$ to $n-1$ gives $H_n-\log(n+1)$ because the logarithmic ratios telescope.</details>

Explore the local transition and its quadratic information geometry. {{interactive_demo:1}} {{visualization:0}}

